cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use padaquad in your work, please cite the software as below."
type: software
title: "padaquad: parallel adaptive numerical quadrature in PyTorch"
abstract: >-
  padaquad computes definite integrals of functions that can be evaluated, in
  PyTorch. It splits the integration domain into subintervals, refines those
  whose error estimate is too large, and evaluates the integrand at many points
  of many subintervals in one call, on a CPU or a GPU, with gradients through
  the result.
authors:
  - family-names: Hegazy
    given-names: Kareem
# version equals pyproject.toml, and date-released equals that version's date in
# CHANGELOG.md; tests/test_docs_methods_table.py checks both.
version: "1.3.0"
date-released: "2026-11-10"
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/khegazy/padaquad"
url: "https://khegazy.github.io/padaquad/"
keywords:
  - numerical integration
  - adaptive quadrature
  - Gauss-Kronrod
  - Clenshaw-Curtis
  - PyTorch
  - automatic differentiation
